~Version ---------------------------------------------------
VERS.   2.0 : CWLS log ASCII Standard -VERSION 2.0
WRAP.    NO : One line per depth step
DLM . SPACE : Column Data Section Delimiter
~Well ------------------------------------------------------
STRT.M              3071.6 : START DEPTH
STOP.M              3180.1 : STOP DEPTH
STEP.M                   0 : STEP
NULL.              -999.25 : NULL VALUE
COMP.          Norsk Hydro : COMPANY
WELL.             35/11-13 : WELL
FLD .                      : FIELD
LOC .                      : LOCATION
PROV.                      : PROVINCE
CNTY.                      : COUNTY
STAT.                      : STATE
CTRY.                      : COUNTRY
SRVC. Schlumberger MDT CQG : SERVICE COMPANY
DATE.                      : DATE
UWI .                      : UNIQUE WELL ID
API .                      : API NUMBER
~Curve Information -----------------------------------------
DEPT    .M                            : TVD below MSL, positive down
MD      .M                            : Measured depth from RKB
PRES    .BAR                          : MDT CQG formation pressure
TEST    .                             : Original test number
MUDPRE  .BAR                          : Mud pressure before, not formation pressure
MUDPOST .BAR                          : Mud pressure after
MOBILITY.MD/CP                        : Mobility
FLUID   . : Report-interpreted branch : 1 gas 2 oil 3 water
QC      .            : Report quality : 0 ok 1 low mobility 2 dry
USE_FIT .                             : 1 include in oil-water fit, 0 exclude
~Params ----------------------------------------------------
DREF  .               TVD MSL : Positive down; first index is TVD, not measured depth
SOURCE. NH/OD-B-4522/05 Rev 1 : 2005-12-13; PDF p54 Table 3.7.4
PREF  .           AS REPORTED : Table specifies bar, not absolute/gauge reference
FLDMAP.   1=gas;2=oil;3=water : Explicit FLUID curve code mapping
~Other -----------------------------------------------------
Irregular stations; STEP=0. No resampling. CSV retains zones and remarks.
Fluid labels are report interpretations, not samples at every depth. See README.md.
